ork by local artists and artisans and operates an associated gallery at 112 W. Alabama Avenue.","source_url":"https://www.rustonlincoln.com/directory/creative-exchange/","source_title":"Creative Exchange | Experience Ruston","source_kind":"government","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Marketplace address is 301 N. Trenton St.; gallery programming is periodic, so confirm exhibits or workshops in advance.","cost_status":"purchase_required","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"lincoln-parish-museum-n-vienna-st","subject_type":"street_or_district","entity_name":"Lincoln Parish Museum","title":"Read the Parish Through Its Artifacts","subtitle":"North Vienna Street corridor","notes":"Look for the period furnishings, photographs, clothing, and seven Walls That Talk murals inside the 1886 Kidd-Davis home.","short_summary":"A historic house museum interpreting Lincoln Parish through objects and murals.","evidence_claim":"The Lincoln Parish Museum at 609 N. Vienna Street occupies the 1886 Kidd-Davis home and displays period artifacts plus seven history murals with recorded stories.","source_url":"https://www.rustonlincoln.com/directory/lincoln-parish-museum/","source_title":"Lincoln Parish Museum | Experience Ruston","source_kind":"cultural_institution","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Located at 609 N. Vienna St.; confirm public opening times and any admission requirements before visiting.","cost_status":"unknown","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"dixie-center-n-vienna-st","subject_type":"street_or_district","entity_name":"Dixie Center for the Arts","title":"Check the Historic Dixie Stage","subtitle":"North Vienna Street corridor","notes":"Review the performance calendar before walking over; community theater, concerts, and other programmed events use this restored venue.","short_summary":"A re